# TODO - Differential VM verification

## Objective

Run specification fixtures through the Rust VM, independent C VM, and
accelerator VM and compare output, termination, state, mutation, and instruction
traces. Run the original C interpreter only on the documented agreement subset
as historical differential evidence.

## Acceptance

- The Rust VM, independent C VM, and any accelerator VM agree with the normative
  specification on all admitted classic fixtures. The historical interpreter
  participates only for fixtures whose behavior is defined and documented to
  agree with the specification.
- The verifier is tested against valid cases and deliberately mutated invalid
  cases so acceptance and rejection boundaries are evidenced independently.
- The declared scope contains no unresolved placeholder implementation or
  undocumented workaround required for this objective to function.
- Evidence is durable enough to move this TODO to `docs/todo/completed/` and
  remove the exact TODO heading without losing unfinished intent.

## Evidence

- Current Rust/C semantic-signature evidence covers arithmetic, loading, I/O,
  mutation, pointer behavior, termination, and atomic rejection.
- Generated classic/profiled differential cases compare complete 59,049-word
  memory images with deterministic replay and progressive shrinking.
- CUDA compact-step and resident classic/current suites compare complete
  observable state against normative Rust, including full memory images.
- The integrated exact candidate verifier rejects a mutated C signature and a
  single unproved candidate, and complete CUDA checkpoints use the same
  boundary.

- Durable evidence includes the exact labeled-candidate verifier, complete
  Rust/C and CUDA observations, generated full-memory cases, seeded mutation,
  single-candidate rejection, sanitizer bounds, and deterministic replay.
- Prerequisite completion evidence: `safe-rust-malbolge-vm`,
  `independent-pure-c-malbolge-vm`, `reference-interpreter-sanitizer-harness`.
- **Completion:** Completed on 2026-08-06 after exact labeled-candidate
  verification, Rust/independent-C signature agreement, mutated-signature and
  insufficient-candidate rejection, full-state CUDA classic/current comparison,
  generated replay/shrink evidence, sanitizer bounds, Clippy, tests, and Jig
  validation passed.
